      title: 'Paston',
      subtitle: 'Trick-taking',
    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Paston',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Paston is a three-player Armenian Preference-style trick-taking game from Gyumri. The declarer chooses trumps after bidding and must take at least six of ten tricks or surrender.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Rooted in the interaction between Eastern European trick-taking traditions and Middle Eastern social gaming. It bears strong similarities to 'Pastushok' and 'Preferans'.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Three players; no partnerships. The game is played mainly in Armenia (e.g. Gyumri). Deal, bidding and play are clockwise; each player plays for themselves toward 121 points.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32 cards (remove 2s through 6s).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32 cards (remove 2s through 6s).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Each player receives 10 cards (often dealt 2 at a time). 2 cards are placed face-down in the 'Prikup'.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Score when declarer surrenders: In some rules opponents do not score 2 points when the declarer surrenders; in others they do. Affects whether sacrifice bids are more attractive.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Paston grkha (best spades): Highest bid; spades are trump but with higher penalty for losing. Declarer scores only +10 for six tricks (not multiplied by 4); other scores multiplied by 4.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Redeal conditions: If bottom card is 7 of spades, cards are reshuffled and redealt. If a player holds 7-8-9-10-J-Q of spades but neither K nor A of spades, cards are shown and redealt by same dealer.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
